TASK:
You are given a set and other sets.
Your job is to find whether set is a strict superset of each of the sets.
Print True, if is a strict superset of each of the sets. Otherwise, print False.
A strict superset has at least one element that does not exist in its subset. 
PROGRAM:
# Read the main set A
A = set(map(int, input().split()))

# Read the number of other sets
num_other_sets = int(input())

# Variable to keep track of the result
is_strict_superset = True

for _ in range(num_other_sets):
    other_set = set(map(int, input().split()))
    
    # A is a strict superset if A contains all elements of other_set AND A is larger than other_set
    if not (A.issuperset(other_set) and len(A) > len(other_set)):
        is_strict_superset = False
        break

print(is_strict_superset)
